---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro"
import PageFooter from "../components/PageFooter.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service | Packstack" description="Terms of Service for Packstack: the rules for using our gear list and pack weight platform.">
  <div class="bg-background min-h-screen">
    <PageHeader />

    <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-12 prose prose-invert prose-sm">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-1">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-label text-sm mt-0 mb-10">Effective Date: October 9, 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        Packstack, LLC ("Packstack," "we," "us," or "our") operates the website
        <a href="https://www.packstack.io">www.packstack.io</a>, the web application at
        <a href="https://app.packstack.io">app.packstack.io</a>, and the Packstack mobile apps for
        iOS and Android (collectively, the "Service").
      </p>
      <p>
        By using the Service, you agree to these Terms of Service ("Terms") and to our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the Service. You must
        be at least 13 years old to use the Service, and by using it you confirm that you are.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The Service</h2>
      <p>
        Packstack is a gear list and pack weight platform for backpackers and hikers. It lets you
        build a gear closet, create and share packing lists, plan trips, track pack weight, and
        connect AI assistants to your account, through our website, web app, and mobile apps.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        Most features require an account. You can sign in with a one-time code sent to your email
        address, or with Google or Apple. You are responsible for keeping access to your email and
        sign-in accounts secure, and for all activity under your Packstack account. Tell us right
        away at <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a> if you suspect
        unauthorized use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each person may have only one account. We may suspend or remove duplicate accounts.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Packstack Pro and Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Packstack offers a free tier and a paid tier, Packstack Pro. Pro is available as a monthly
        subscription, an annual subscription, or a one-time purchase. The price and what Pro
        includes are shown before you buy, and may vary by platform and region. We may change the
        limits of the free tier and the features included in Pro over time.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Purchases through the App Store or Google Play.</strong> These are billed to your
        Apple or Google account. Subscriptions renew automatically at the end of each period unless
        you turn off auto-renewal at least 24 hours before the period ends. You can manage or
        cancel them in your App Store or Google Play account settings; deleting the app or your
        Packstack account does not cancel them. Refunds are handled by Apple or Google under their
        policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Purchases on the web.</strong> These are billed through our payment processor.
        Subscriptions renew automatically at the end of each period until you cancel. You can
        cancel at any time from Settings in the web app, under Manage subscription. Except where
        the law requires otherwise, web purchases are non-refundable, and we do not give prorated
        refunds for partial periods.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cancellation.</strong> When you cancel a subscription, you keep Pro until the end
        of the period you have paid for.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>One-time purchase.</strong> A one-time purchase is not a subscription and does not
        renew. It unlocks Pro on your account for as long as we offer Packstack Pro.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Price changes.</strong> We may change subscription prices. We will give you at
        least 30 days' notice before a new price applies to your subscription, and the App Store
        and Google Play may also ask you to agree to the change. If you do not want to pay the new
        price, cancel before it takes effect.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Your Content</h2>
      <p>
        "Your Content" means anything you create, upload, or store in the Service, including gear,
        packing lists, trips, photos, and notes.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Ownership.</strong> You own Your Content.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>License to us.</strong> You give Packstack a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free
        license to host, store, display, reproduce, and distribute Your Content only as needed to
        operate and provide the Service.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Sharing.</strong> When you share a trip, anyone with the link can view it. Trips
        you publish may appear in public listings and in search engines, and your public profile
        can be viewed by anyone. You are responsible for what you choose to share.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Removal.</strong> We may remove content that violates these Terms or that we
        reasonably believe is harmful or objectionable.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Estimates Are Not Advice</h2>
      <p>
        Packstack shows estimates to help you plan, including calorie, food, and water targets,
        trail distances, elevation, terrain, and expected temperatures, product weights and
        specifications, and over-packing warnings. Some of this information is researched
        automatically, including with AI, and may be incomplete or wrong.
      </p>
      <p>
        These estimates are for general planning only. They are not medical, nutritional, or
        safety advice. Backpacking and hiking carry real risks. Check trail and weather conditions
        with authoritative sources, carry enough food and water for your own needs, and consult a
        qualified professional about your health. You are responsible for your own preparation and
        safety.
      </p>

      <h2>7. AI Assistants and Other Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        You can connect AI assistants, such as Claude or ChatGPT, to your Packstack account. When
        you do, you authorize that assistant to read your data and, if you have Pro, to make
        changes on your behalf, such as adding gear or building packs. Changes an assistant makes
        are treated as changes you made. You can disconnect an assistant at any time in Settings
        under Connected apps.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Service may also link to or work with other third-party websites and services. We do
        not control them and are not responsible for their content, products, or services. Your use
        of them is governed by their own terms and policies.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use the Service to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Violate any applicable law or regulation</li>
        <li>Impersonate any person or entity, or misrepresent your affiliation with any person or entity</li>
        <li>Upload or transmit viruses, malware, or other harmful code</li>
        <li>
          Scrape, crawl, or use automated means to access the Service without our written consent,
          except through features we provide for that purpose, such as connecting an AI assistant
        </li>
        <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or disassemble any part of the Service</li>
        <li>Interfere with or disrupt the integrity or performance of the Service</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of the Service or its related systems</li>
        <li>Use the Service for any commercial purpose not expressly permitted by these Terms</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate your account if we reasonably believe you have violated any of
        these restrictions.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        The Service, including its design, graphics, user interface, logos, trademarks, and
        underlying software, belongs to Packstack, LLC and is protected by copyright, trademark,
        and other intellectual property laws. You may not copy, modify, distribute, sell, or lease
        any part of the Service, or reverse-engineer or attempt to extract its source code, unless
        the law permits it or you have our written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Mobile Apps</h2>
      <p>
        Your use of the Packstack mobile apps is also subject to the terms of the store you
        downloaded them from (the Apple App Store or Google Play). If these Terms conflict with
        those store terms, these Terms govern your relationship with Packstack. We do not
        guarantee that the apps will work on every device or operating system version.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND,
        WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
        MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or secure, or that
        defects will be corrected. We do not warrant the accuracy, reliability, or completeness of
        any content or estimate in the Service. You use the Service at your own risk.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, PACKSTACK, LLC AND ITS OFFICERS,
        DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AND AGENTS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
        CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, USE, OR GOODWILL, ARISING
        OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH YOUR USE OF THE SERVICE.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our total liability for any claims arising out of or relating to these Terms or the Service
        shall not exceed the greater of the total amount you paid to Packstack in the twelve (12)
        months before the event giving rise to the claim, or $50.00.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Packstack, LLC and its officers,
        directors, employees, and agents from any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses
        (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or connected with your use of the
        Service, Your Content, or your violation of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the Service at any time, and you can delete your account yourself: in
        the mobile app under Account Details, or on the web in Settings. You can also ask us to
        delete it at <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a>. Deleting your
        account does not cancel an App Store or Google Play subscription.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate your access to the Service at any time, with or without cause
        or notice, including if we reasonably believe you have violated these Terms. When your
        access ends, your right to use the Service ends immediately. We handle deletion of your
        data as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, United States, without
        regard to its conflict-of-law rules.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Dispute Resolution</h2>
      <p>
        If you have a dispute with Packstack about these Terms or the Service, you agree to first
        try to resolve it informally by contacting us at
        <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a>. We will try to resolve it
        within thirty (30) days of receiving your notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        If it is not resolved within that time, either party may bring a claim in the state or
        federal courts located in the State of Delaware, and you and Packstack each consent to the
        exclusive jurisdiction of those courts.
      </p>

      <h2>17. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. If we make material changes, we will update
        the Effective Date above and, where appropriate, notify you in the Service. Your continued
        use of the Service after a change means you accept the updated Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>18. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions or concerns about these Terms, please contact us at:</p>
      <p>
        Packstack, LLC<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a>
      </p>
    </main>

    <PageFooter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
